#. DialogueBefore = Player Default: I will be voting for his execution. I encourage you to do the same. &&& Yeats: That is what Hal wants. But I teeter. I am far too acquainted with man's flaws to inflict such a punishment. &&& Yeats: But I digress. In closing I will leave you with the words of Clarice Lispector:|"Who has not asked himself at some time or other: am I a monster or is this what it means to be a person?"
#. DialogueAfter = Player Default: Well said.
#. EDID: [01027DE4]
#. REC: INFO:NAM1
msgctxt "0008EA"
msgid "People can be monstrous. It's choosing not to, every day, that makes us human."
msgstr "사람은 괴물이 될 수 있습니다. 매일 그렇게 되지 않기로 선택하는 것이 우리를 인간으로 만듭니다."

