#. DialogueBefore = Player Default: Of course. Confessions are between him and God. &&& Yeats: Yes, that would violate the seal of confession. A priest cannot reveal anything that would betray the penitent. &&& Yeats: But now that Hal has come forward, the greater question of course, is what to do about it.
#. DialogueAfter = Player Default: A middle ground. A fair choice for one who plays the part of man and beast.
#. EDID: [01027DC7]
#. REC: INFO:NAM1
msgctxt "0008F9"
msgid "Exile is the best option."
msgstr "추방이 최선의 선택입니다."

#. List: 2
#. QuestName = SFFL_MS01_Quest
#. SceneName = SFFL_MS01_Quest_c2535_TalkToResidents_TL_Yeats
#. DialogCallType = NPCResponse
#. Speaker = Yeats
#. VoiceType = SFFL_MS01_NPCMYeats
#. Face = Neutral
#. SoundFileID = 00338910
#. ScriptNotes = / to Player Default
#. Prompt = Exonerate him. He's paid his debt to society.
#. DialogueBefore = Player Default: Exonerate him. He's paid his debt to society.
#. DialogueAfter = Yeats: But I digress. In closing I will leave you with the words of Clarice Lispector:
#. EDID: [01027DD5]
#. REC: INFO:NAM1
msgctxt "0008FA"
msgid "Fair. I do believe he is a changed man, but my opinion bears no more weight than that of his victims."
msgstr "공정하군요. 저는 그가 변한 사람이라고 믿지만, 제 의견이 피해자들의 의견보다 더 무게를 갖지는 않습니다."

#. List: 2
#. QuestName = SFFL_MS01_Quest
#. SceneName = SFFL_MS01_Quest_c2535_TalkToResidents_TL_Yeats
#. DialogCallType = PlayerDialogue
#. Speaker = Player
#. Alias = Yeats
#. VoiceType = PlayerVoiceMale01 / PlayerVoiceFemale01
#. Face = Neutral
